    "title": "Outpatient Maintenance of Chronic Schizophrenic Patients with Long-acting Fluphenazine: Double-blind Placebo Trial",
    "authors": "S. R. HIRSCH, R. GAIND, P. D. ROHDE, B. C. STEVENS, J. K. WING",
    "year": "1973",
    "journal": "British Medical Journal",
    "country": "United Kingdom",
    "doi": null,
    "study_design": "Double-blind placebo-controlled randomized trial; randomization was performed by a research assistant as patients entered the trial.",
    "inclusion_criteria": "Chronic schizophrenic outpatients who had been maintained on fluphenazine decanoate injections for eight or more weeks; current age 15-67; age of onset 10-60; positive evidence of schizophrenia in the case records; chronicity indicated by two or more admissions to hospital or one admission lasting more than six months; maintenance on a minimum monthly dose of fluphenazine decanoate of 25 mg begun at least eight weeks before beginning the trial and without supplementary ataractic medication.",
    "exclusion_criteria": "Not schizophrenic; not chronically schizophrenic; too old; irregular attendance; severe alcohol or drug abuse; other anti-psychotic medication.",
    "study_setting": "Special outpatient clinics at St. Olave's Hospital and St. Francis Hospital, London.",
    "source_of_recruitment": "All outpatients attending the catchment area clinic at St. Olave's Hospital and suitable outpatients from St. Francis Hospital, Camberwell.",
